@verbs wear unwear hold wield unhold equip
@tier player
@title dressing, wielding, and equipping in one go
@see get equipment

  wear <item>      anything that is clothing or armour goes on.
  unwear <item>    and off again.

  hold <item>      you take it in your hands to use it.
  unhold <item>    you stop holding it, but still carry it.

You hold one thing in each hand: two weapons, or a weapon and a
shield. Anything that asks for both hands, a staff say, does not go
in until both are free. And only what was made to be held is held.
'wield' does the same as 'hold'.

  equip

With no argument: it walks what you are carrying and puts on and
holds everything that can be put on and held. It is the same thing
the game does for you on entering if your 'autoequiparse' consent
is set to yes.

To see what you are wearing and the state it is in, use
'equipment'.
